      {
        "id": "p19-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the $x$- and $y$-intercepts of the equation $\\dfrac{x}{a}+\\dfrac{y}{b}=1$. What do you notice?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(a,0)$ and $(0,b)$. The intercepts appear in the denominators of the equation.",
          "worked": "For the $x$-intercept, put $y=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{a}+\\frac{0}{b}&=1\\\\\\frac{x}{a}&=1\\\\x&=a.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the $y$-intercept, put $x=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{0}{a}+\\frac{y}{b}&=1\\\\\\frac{y}{b}&=1\\\\y&=b.\\end{align*}$$\nThe intercepts are $(a,0)$ and $(0,b)$: their non-zero coordinates are the respective denominators.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q15-b",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Use the result of part a to sketch these lines quickly.",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 3,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p19-q15-b-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x}{6}-\\dfrac{y}{3}=1$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Straight line through $(6,0)$ and $(0,-3)$.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{6}-\\frac{y}{3}&=1\\\\\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{y}{-3}&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe intercepts are $(6,0)$ and $(0,-3)$. Plot them and draw the straight line through them.",
